C. Baselines
We compare against representative time-series classifiers spanning convolutional, random-kernel and attention/hybrid families: InceptionTime [14], ROCKET/MiniRocket [15], [16], TIMNET [17], TF-FusNet [18], LightCNN [19], MLSTM-FCN and its channel-attention variant CA-MLSTMFCN [20], [21], and TapNet [22]. Results are summarized in Table I.
D. Overall Results
As shown in Table I, ASA-DSNet achieves the best performance across all tasks. On PADS, it reaches 94.37% (PD vs. HC), 86.90% (PD vs. DD), and 80.85% (PD vs. HC vs. DD). On Monipar, it attains 95.17% Accuracy and 96.87% F1. Compared with the strongest baseline (CA-MLSTM-FCN), our method improves by approximately 2 to 4 percentage points on PADS. We attribute the gains to two factors. Firstly, Stage 1 improves class separability via complementary temporal–
